add('How to learn from every concept and example',head('A REPEATABLE LEARNING PATTERN','Understand → observe → change → verify')+'<div class="grid four">'+card('loop-learn','1 · CONCEPT','Build a mental model','What does the SDK provide?<br>What does the host application control?')+card('loop-observe','2 · PRACTICAL APPLICATION','Watch the behavior','Follow the interface, the source<br>and the messages produced by a run.')+card('loop-change','3 · HANDS-ON LAB','Make a small change','Predict the result, adjust one input,<br>and run a bounded experiment.')+card('loop-verify','4 · EVIDENCE','Explain what happened','Inspect the result and tool evidence.<br>Record what you learned and try again.')+'</div>',[('loop-learn','For each concept, begin with the mental model. Ask what the SDK does and what your application remains responsible for.'),('loop-observe','Then watch the paired application. Connect the interface, source code, messages, and visible result.'),('loop-change','Next, make one small change in a lab. Predict the outcome before running it, so the experiment answers a specific question.'),('loop-verify','Finally, inspect the evidence and explain what happened. Progress comes from understanding and verifying the behavior, not just playing the videos.')])
